"""Atlas content for patches 2.1 A Realm Awoken to 2.3 Defenders of Eorzea: MSQ #162 The Price of Principles to
#199 Brave New Companions (steps cp-msq-162 … cp-msq-199). Era tag c.

Data only, per docs/atlas/era-modules.md. Researched 2026-11-19 from the saved Console Games Wiki wikitext (lanes
L01–L05); every locator is an exact substring of the quest's saved page (Journal, Steps or main dialogue).

Spoiler handling in this era:
  - first names only (Teledji, Nanamo, Lolorito, Merlwyb, Yugiri); no surnames, so no "Warde", "Leveilleur",
    "Baelsar" or "Adeledji" in displayed text;
  - Nabriales and Zodiark stay out of displayed text (banned); the Ascian who questions Elidibus is "another Ascian";
  - Teledji's one-word order at #185 is the title of #190, so the text only says he gave an order his servant
    did not understand;
  - the white-robed Ascian is named Elidibus from #170, where the page names him after the vision;
  - Iceheart is her own entry (the page never gives her birthname);
  - the trial company is "Alphinaud's trial company" from #196 and takes its name, the Crystal Braves, at #199.
"""

def P(frm, until, scope, name, summary, claims, aliases=()):
    return dict(frm=frm, until=until, scope=scope, name=name, aliases=list(aliases), summary=summary, claims=claims)

T = {n: f"cp-msq-{n}" for n in range(162, 200)}
ANT = ["the Antecedent"]

